      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\n`safetensors.torch.load_file` maps a file through `UntypedStorage.from_file(shared=False)` — a private, writable mapping. On a shared CPU/GPU pool that permission costs memory, which `runtime/loader/readonly_safetensors.py` already documents for the checkpoint path:\r\n\r\n> when the device copies from such a mapping the driver pins the pages with write intent, the kernel breaks copy-on-write, and every page copied becomes anonymous memory — 1 GiB copied in 1 GiB of unreclaimable RAM, at a fraction of the bandwidth.\r\n\r\nThat loader was added for the ordinary checkpoint mapping, but the LoRA merge cache still reads through `safetensors_load_file` at both of its read sites. A merged adapter is written once by `save_file` + `os.replace` and is immutable afterwards, so it never needs the write permission — yet every co-resident instance that reads it currently pays for a private copy.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nBoth read sites use the existing `load_safetensors_readonly`, and the now-unused `safetensors_load_file` import is dropped. No API, dependency, or configuration change.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nNot applicable in the usual sense: the bytes returned are identical, only the mapping permission changes. Sanity check performed — two co-resident instances reading the same merge-cache key return identical tensors, and a request through the merged adapter is unaffected.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNo speed claim. This is a host-memory change only.\r\n\r\nMiniMax-H3 fl2va, one RTX PRO 6000 (SM120), `--layerwise-offload-components dit,text_encoder,image_encoder`, merge cache ~62 GiB:\r\n\r\n| | Pss |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| instance A alone | 167.11 GiB |\r\n| instance A after B joined (same merge-cache key) | **145.81 GiB** |\r\n\r\n≈42.6 GiB of the cache stops being a private copy per instance.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). — `pre-commit run --files ...` passes all hooks on the changed file.\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests — not included. This is a two-call-site loader swap; I am happy to add a mock-based regression test asserting the read path goes through the read-only loader if you would like one.\r\n- [x] Update documentation — no user-visible behavior or configuration change.\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results — see the sections above; no speed or accuracy delta is claimed.\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\nHappy to work with the Merge Oncall and Codeowners on review. The change is deliberately minimal so it can land independently of the layerwise-offload sharing work; it is the same placement this repository already made for the checkpoint path.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37875268406](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37875268406)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37875268108](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37875268108)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37875268351](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37875268351)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
